    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-History--North-Las-Vegas-Campus_R0154048": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History, North Las Vegas Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of History with an emphasis on US and/or State constitutions. The Assistant Professor of History will primarily teach in-person sections of HIST 101, HIST 102, CH 203 and PSC 101 at our new North Las Vegas Campus, with opportunities to teach additional courses within our History program . Please review our catalog for course descriptions here: Nevada State University Catalogs - Course Descriptions.   Appointment to this position is contingent upon confirmed funding and facility readiness at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. In the event of a delayed campus opening, the University reserves the right to adjust course modality and/or location including to the Henderson campus. The primary location for this position is the North Las Vegas campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses online and/or at Nevada State University's Henderson campus. About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   The History Program at Nevada State: The history major at Nevada State University is housed within the Department of History, Law, and Society. The degree program offers two tracks: a traditional history degree and a history degree with a concentration in pre-law. The program also serves students who are seeking history for secondary education degrees. The program encourages hands-on learning of historical methods and emphasizes a capstone senior seminar experience where students conduct their own primary source research. In addition, the history program serves the general Nevada State University student population through its lower-level general education-oriented courses.   About the Institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving Institution (MSI) with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching, and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: Teach core Nevada State University courses in history, core humanities, and political science in-person format at the North Las Vegas campus. The 9-month teaching load is 4 courses per semester (fall and spring), also known as a 4/4 load. New faculty receive two course releases in their first year. Recruit new students into the history and history pre-law degree programs. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in History. Candidates who are ABD are eligible with the expectation that the Ph.D. will be completed by July 31, 2027. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the college or university level as evidenced by student evaluations of courses, teaching awards, and other markers. Ability to teach the following courses: HIST 101, HIST 102, CH 203, and PSC 101. A sincere interest in joining a teaching university devoted to providing opportunities for a largely underserved population, including non-traditional and first-generation college students. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Expertise in United States and/or State Constitution(s).   Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $62,000.00. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, November 16, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 15 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Part-Time-Instructor---TRIO-Upward-Bound_R0154073": {
      "title": "Part Time Instructor - TRIO Upward Bound",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Part Time Instructor - TRIO Upward Bound. This position will work with two of Nevada State University's TRIO Upward Bound grants that serve eligible students from CCSD high schools. We are searching for individuals with experience teaching in the following high school subjects: Math (e.g., Algebra I, Algebra II, Geometry, Trigonometry, Precalculus, Calculus) English Earth, Biological and Physical Sciences Computer Science/Coding/Information Technology Financial Literacy College Readiness ACT/SAT Preparation The program runs from November to April. Some staff may be hired for a shorter period depending on the training and operations needs of the programs. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else. Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White. We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada. We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community. We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education. Core Responsibilities Develop lesson plans. Provide instruction that leads to success in high school and college. Complete individual student assessments. Classroom management. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Recent teaching experience, preferably with secondary education students. The TRIO Upward Bound faculty and staff work with children. All employees must be able to pass a Nevada State University and Clark County School District background check. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching Advanced Placement courses. Certification is strongly desired. Work Hours: 4 hours per week. Hourly Rate: $27.00 per hour (contingent upon grant funding). Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site. If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  No Full-Time Equivalent 10.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .  Please upload the following documents: Detailed resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Cover Letter indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Names and contact information of three references (you will be notified before references are contacted). Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date 06/30/2027 Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Physical-Sciences_R0154049": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Physical Sciences within the Department of Physical and Life Sciences (PaLS) beginning fall 2027. The Assistant Professor of Physical Sciences will have a specialization in a field offered within our core curriculum: Geology, Meteorology or Climatology, Environmental Science, or Physics. We hope to find a colleague with interest and potential to participate in interdisciplinary opportunities in curriculum development and research among faculty and students and support the curriculum of our new branch campus.   The primary location for this position is Nevada State University's Henderson campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus . About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   About the Department of Physical and Life Sciences at Nevada State: The selected faculty candidate will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team, supporting Bachelor of Science degrees in Biology, Chemistry, Environmental Science, and Human Health Sciences. We value excellence in teaching and hope to find a colleague with an interest and potential to participate in interdisciplinary opportunities in curriculum development and research among faculty and students.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: This is a 9-month appointment assigned 24 credits per academic year, which equates to approximately 12 credit hours in the fall semester and 12 credit hours in the spring semester. A 3-credit release is provided each semester for the first year. Teach at both North Las Vegas and Henderson campuses. Teach lower-level courses in Geology, Environmental Science, Meteorology or Climatology, Physics, or Astronomy with the potential to develop courses (lower- and upper-level) in an area of specialization that may complement other degrees in the department in a mostly in-person format. Create a culture of inclusive learning. Faculty at Nevada State put our students’ needs at the forefront of curriculum design and classroom experiences. This includes classroom policies, management, and pedagogical practices that amplify the shared cultural capital of our diverse student body and acknowledge their lived experience. Faculty maintain a learning environment that actively avoids racism, sexism, ableism, and discrimination due to sexual orientation. This is an equally shared responsibility irrespective of the identity of the faculty member. Engage in institutional service. This may involve contributing to the development of programmatic goals and shared self-governance on campus in a variety of roles. For example, faculty may serve in faculty senate positions, contribute to curriculum design, advise on policy development, and/or participate in program assessment. Engage in professional development activities. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning.   Required Qualifications: Terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D.) in any Physical Sciences field at the time of employment. Evidence of strong commitment to teaching, mentoring, and working with undergraduates. Demonstrated commitment to a diverse, non-traditional, first-generation student population. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas). Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of instructional effectiveness at the college/university level. Commitment to active/experiential learning. Experience or interest in developing curriculum at the university level. Evidence of scholarly productivity and potential. Experience in mentoring Undergraduate Researchers.   Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is commensurate with experience. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Thursday, November 12, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 11 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Visual-Media--Henderson-Campus_R0153998": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Visual Media, Henderson Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Visual Media. This 9-month, tenure-track position will teach in one or more areas covered by the program. This is primarily a production position; expertise in film or media studies is valued, but secondary to production skills.   Teaching assignments are primarily located at Nevada State University's Henderson campus and are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs, and they may include courses online and/or at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   About the Visual Media Program at Nevada State: The Visual Media program includes four concentrations: Animation, 3D Animation, Digital Cinema, and Photo/Documentary. The program features forward-looking curriculum design with emphasis on moving students into specialized paths and support for successful portfolio creation. It is also anchored by a theoretical foundation that approaches film and animation from an experiential perspective, and includes instruction in AI that helps students navigate the quickly evolving tools and changing media landscape affected by AI.   Students move through dedicated course sequences for each concentration. Other notable classes include Animation Studio, a class introducing students to industry workflows and producing for animation; Physics of Media Creation, which instructs students in the physics of light, optics, sound, and movement as part of the core curriculum; and Film Music and Scoring, which introduces students to digital tools and basic music principles, equipping them to score their own works.    The Visual Media program has small class sizes, with most production classes topping out at twenty seats. We teach using the Adobe Creative Cloud, Davinci Resolve, Toon Boom, Blender, Unreal Engine, Storyboard Pro, Reaper, and other software platforms; we are also open to new platforms as introduced by the successful candidate.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teach upper- or lower-division courses in one or more of the following areas: 2D Animation (rigged puppet with some hand-drawn) 3D Animation Audio recording / Audio postproduction Cinematography Documentary production Editing Film production Photography Producing Screenwriting Storyboarding Visual Effects Serve on departmental and college-wide committees and support the program and institution through service contributions. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline, creative scholarship, or in the scholarship of teaching and learning.   Required Qualifications: MFA or terminal degree in animation, film, or similar. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).   Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of teaching excellence at the college level. Strong portfolio of creative work. Animation is our primary growth area, so candidates with a background in animation are encouraged to apply.   Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $61,872.00. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, November 30, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 29 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Creative Portfolio; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Visual-Media--North-Las-Vegas-Campus_R0154044-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Visual Media, North Las Vegas Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Visual Media. This position will support Fine Arts core instruction with an emphasis in Visual Media at the new North Las Vegas campus.   Appointment to this position is contingent upon confirmed funding and facility readiness at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. In the event of a delayed campus opening, the University reserves the right to adjust course modality and/or location including to the Henderson campus. The primary location for this position is the North Las Vegas campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include online courses and/or courses at Nevada State University's Henderson campus. About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   About the Visual Media program at Nevada State: The Visual Media program includes concentrations in Animation, 3D Animation, Digital Cinema, and Photo/Documentary, and serves the university core through select courses. About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teach lower-division courses in areas related to the Fine Arts core with an emphasis in Visual Media; subject areas may include the following, according to candidate specialties (it is not expected that candidates will be able to teach in all areas): Art (visual foundations, drawing, art appreciation, art history, sculpture) Photography Film studies (survey of film, film history, film language) 3D printing Possible coursework in film music, media creation, or areas related to the above Serve on departmental and college-wide committees and perform other service at the university or departmental levels. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning.   Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in the field of Visual Media. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).   Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Demonstration of teaching excellence at the collegiate level.   Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $61,872.00 Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, November 30, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 29 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-English--North-Las-Vegas-Campus_R0154047": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English, North Las Vegas Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of English. The Assistant Professor of English will have a special passion for engaging with first year students as well as teaching writing across academic contexts. This position will primarily teach our First-Year Composition curriculum at our new campus in North Las Vegas, with opportunities to teach additional courses within our English B.A. program, in either in-person or online formats.  Although this position will be housed in the English department, it will also support the First-Year Experience program at Nevada State on an as-needed basis (approximately 50% of the workload).   Appointment to this position is contingent upon confirmed funding and facility readiness at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. In the event of a delayed campus opening, the University reserves the right to adjust course modality and/or location including to the Henderson campus. The primary location for this position is the North Las Vegas campus. T eaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include courses online and/or at Nevada State University's Henderson campus. About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   About English Department at Nevada State: The selected faculty candidate will join a collaborative and interdisciplinary team, supporting the Bachelor of Arts degree in English and the First-Year Composition program. While teaching is the primary focus at Nevada State, the selected faculty candidates would be expected to engage in scholarly activities (within their discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning). Faculty in our department collaborate on school and campus-wide initiatives, and they often serve on local, regional, and national committees in their respective areas. Our faculty also share a deep commitment to innovating teaching practices, supporting undergraduate research, and mentoring students.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teach core Nevada State University courses in First Year Composition and First Year Experience in a face-to-face format at our North Las Vegas campus. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity or in the scholarship of teaching and learning. Collaborate with colleagues to promote writing within and across the curriculum.   Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in in Composition and Rhetoric, Writing Studies, Literacy Education, English or related field ( candidates who are ABD are eligible with the expectation that the Ph.D. will be completed by July 31, 2027 ); training in or significant experience with composition pedagogy if degree is in a related field. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, especially in first year or lower division courses. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).   Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Ability to teach in a variety of formats (e.g., in-person, hybrid, online). Experience working with underrepresented, first generation, or nontraditional college students. Experience teaching multilingual writers. Knowledge of writing pedagogy, critical pedagogy, and/or other current pedagogies in composition.   Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $62,000.00 Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Wednesday, November 18 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 17 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered. Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
    },
    "https://nshe.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/NSU-external/job/NSU---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Mathematics--North-Las-Vegas-Campus_R0154046": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics, North Las Vegas Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nNevada State University appreciates your interest in employment. To ensure your application process runs smoothly, we ask that you keep in mind the following when completing your application: The required documents are listed below on the posting. Your application may not be considered if you do not attach the required documents. Draft applications are saved automatically and can be accessed through your candidate home account. Completed applications must be submitted prior to the close of the recruitment. Once a recruitment has closed, applications will no longer be accepted. Please note, recruitment will close without notice when a hiring decision has been made. If you need assistance or have questions regarding the application process, please contact the Human Resources department at (702) 992-2320 or apply@nevadastate.edu . Job Description Nevada State University invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Mathematics. The Assistant Professor of Mathematics will be the first full-time mathematics position our new North Las Vegas campus, which is scheduled to open in Fall 2027. Candidates should expect to teach primarily core mathematics courses as the new campus establishes its identity.   Appointment to this position is contingent upon confirmed funding and facility readiness at Nevada State University's North Las Vegas campus. In the event of a delayed campus opening, the University reserves the right to adjust course modality and/or location including to the Henderson campus. The primary location for this position is the North Las Vegas campus. Teaching assignments are determined based on departmental and programmatic needs and may include online courses and/or courses at Nevada State University's Henderson campus.   About the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business at Nevada State: With talented faculty and bold academic programs, the School of Liberal Arts, Sciences, and Business’ (LASB) student-centered ethos cultivates civically-engaged scientists, humanists, business professionals, and artists ready to influence the Southern Nevada region and beyond. Through 6 dynamic Departments - Business; Data, Media, and Design; History, Law, and Society; Humanities; Physical and Life Sciences; and, Psychology and Counseling - LASB educates students through the core curriculum, 21 bachelor’s programs, and 27 minor programs.   About the Mathematics program at Nevada State: The mathematics faculty teach as part of the Department of Data, Media, and Design. This unique faculty cohort creates an opportunity for innovative collaborations across typically noninteracting disciplines, and consists of faculty from Mathematics, Data Science, Communications, and Visual Media. Aside from teaching core mathematics courses for the campus, the faculty teach curriculum to serve both the Mathematics major (BS in Mathematics) and the Secondary Education with a Concentration in Mathematics (BS in Education). We also teach courses for an Applied Statistics minor.   About the institution: Nevada State University, a four-year Minority Serving public institution with a statewide mission, is dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and largely underserved student population. Designated a Hispanic Serving (HSI) and Asian American Native American Pacific Islander Institution (AANAPI), Nevada State is a university where teaching and student support are valued above all else.   Nevada State University continues to grow as an institution of higher education. In Fall 2025, the enrollment surpassed 8,400, with 8,287 undergraduate students and 117 graduate students. A majority of our students are first generation, racial/ethnic minorities, parents, and/or returning students, of which 48% are Hispanic, 10% are Asian/Pacific Islander, 10% are Black/African American, and 22% are White.   We celebrate the storied backgrounds of our campus community. We operate with a shared commitment to represent and serve the diverse population of Nevada and to encourage the exchange of ideas that respects and honors the lived experiences of our students, staff, and faculty. We foster a culture of inclusive excellence so our members can live authentically, fully engage, and flourish. In order to strengthen the university and progress its mission, the university dedicates itself to intentional and ongoing reflection to meeting the evolving needs of Nevada State University, the surrounding communities, and the State of Nevada.   We seek applicants who are passionate about working with this promising student population and collaborating with faculty and staff across departments to make a lasting impact in developing our institution and our community.    We encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Primary Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits per academic year, which amounts to four courses per semester. Teach primarily core mathematics courses until the campus becomes more established. Serve on departmental and college-wide committees. Engage in scholarly activity within your discipline or in the scholarship of teaching and learning.   Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Mathematics or closely related field. Candidates who are ABD are eligible with the expectation that the Ph.D. will be completed by July 31, 2027. Eligibility to work in the United States without sponsorship (Nevada State does not sponsor employment-related visas).   Please note: Applicants must meet the posted minimum qualifications at the time of application in order to be considered for the position.   Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated dedication to or interest in working with a diverse student population. A flexible and entrepreneurial mindset to navigate the challenges of being the inaugural faculty member at a satellite campus.      Rank, Salary & Benefits: 9-month. Tenure Track. Budgeted salary for this position is $63,000.00. Nevada State University offers excellent benefits, including 19.25% retirement match, beginning balance of 30 sick leave days, 12 paid holidays, educational benefits, and three health insurance plans that can be supplemented with flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts.   This Posting is Open Until Filled The posting will remain open until filled, with the first review of applications to begin on Monday, November 30, 2026 . Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply by November 29 for full consideration.   Special Instructions for Internal NSHE Applicants Nevada State University employees or employees within the Nevada System of Higher Education (NSHE, UNLV, UNR, NSU, CSN, TMCC, WNC, GBC, or DRI) MUST use the “Browse Jobs” process within Workday to find and apply for jobs at Nevada State and other NSHE Institutions. Once you log into Workday, type \"Browse Jobs\" in the search box which will navigate to the internal job posting site.   If you complete an application outside of the internal application process, your application will be returned and you will have to reapply as an internal applicant which may delay your application. Exempt  Yes Full-Time Equivalent 100.0% Required Attachment(s) Please note, once you submit your application the only attachment(s) viewable to you will be the attachment(s) to the resume/CV section of the application. Any additional required attachment(s) to the cover letter, references, additional documents sections of the application, will not be viewable to you after you submit your application. All uploaded attachment(s) will be on the application for the committee to review. To request updates to attachments, prior to the committee review of applications, please contact the candidate helpdesk at apply@nevadastate.edu .   Please upload the following documents: Detailed CV or resume listing relevant qualifications and experience; Letter of interest indicating why you are a good fit for the position and Nevada State University; Statement of Teaching Philosophy; Names and contact information of three references, at least one of whom can speak to your teaching ability (you will be notified before references are contacted).   The search committee may ask for more materials at later stages in the application process.   Throughout your application materials, we encourage you to highlight your background in fostering an inclusive campus culture and supporting the success of students who are historically underrepresented in higher education.   Applications that do not include the required uploaded documents may not be considered.     Posting Close Date Note to Applicant Applicants should fully describe their qualifications and experience with specific reference to each of the minimum and preferred qualifications in their cover letter. The search committee will use this information during the initial review of application materials.    References will be contacted at the appropriate phase of the recruitment process.    This position may require a criminal background check to be conducted on the candidate(s) selected for hire.    As part of the hiring process, applicants for positions in the Nevada System of Higher Education may be required to demonstrate the ability to perform job-related tasks.    Nevada State University does not currently sponsor Visas, all applicants must be eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship. Nevada State University"
